WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.770
oato ga mata yoroshikute

00:00.000 --> 00:02.770
Thank you kindly for your attention

00:02.770 --> 00:05.630
osaki mo mae mo yoroshiku ne

00:02.770 --> 00:05.630
I hope to have it again and again

00:05.630 --> 00:08.440
chin-ton chin-ton-shan

00:05.630 --> 00:08.440
Twing-twang twing-twang-twong

00:10.940 --> 00:13.450
jounai manjou

00:10.940 --> 00:13.450
The theater's full

00:17.080 --> 00:19.580
nazotoki dokidoki shinan

00:17.080 --> 00:19.580
Mysteries are fun

00:19.580 --> 00:22.410
shikake ga ariari desu

00:19.580 --> 00:22.410
Tricks are fun as well

00:22.410 --> 00:26.660
joshiteki onayami wa sugoroku sai wo futte

00:22.410 --> 00:26.660
We can solve girly problems by throwing a dice

00:26.660 --> 00:27.380
(hai hai)

00:26.660 --> 00:27.380
(really?)

00:27.380 --> 00:29.230
ichi de mo roku de mo nain

00:27.380 --> 00:29.230
It's not one nor six, but nine

00:29.230 --> 00:29.960
(sou kai)

00:29.230 --> 00:29.960
(really?)

00:29.960 --> 00:31.830
ichi kake bachi ka de sain

00:29.960 --> 00:31.830
The stakes are high, but you can get a sign

00:32.590 --> 00:36.530
hanashi no tsunagari ga miemasen ne

00:32.590 --> 00:36.530
I don't really see how that's related

00:36.530 --> 00:41.690
oya omoshiroku narisou na yokan wa

00:36.530 --> 00:41.690
See, this looks like it's gonna be fun

00:40.840 --> 00:42.630
(oya oya desu)

00:40.840 --> 00:42.630
(see, see?)

00:41.690 --> 00:45.940
me no sakkaku desu ka

00:41.690 --> 00:45.940
Or am I just seeing things?

00:45.940 --> 00:48.710
iya soredemo kamawanai

00:45.940 --> 00:48.710
I don't even care

00:48.710 --> 00:51.690
hai minna

00:48.710 --> 00:51.690
Come on, everyone

00:51.690 --> 00:53.820
mawatte

00:51.690 --> 00:53.820
Let's spin!

00:55.110 --> 00:57.410
omote mo ura uragaeshite

00:55.110 --> 00:57.410
Front and back, let's just turn it around

00:57.410 --> 01:00.160
dondengaeshi mo yoshiyoshi

00:57.410 --> 01:00.160
You can turn the story upside down too

01:00.160 --> 01:02.750
osaki ni ikou saa douzo

01:00.160 --> 01:02.750
Let's go on, ladies first

01:02.750 --> 01:04.870
osaki mo mae mo yoroshiku ne

01:02.750 --> 01:04.870
I hope to see you around again and again

01:04.870 --> 01:07.760
ura butai ga hare butai de

01:04.870 --> 01:07.760
The backstage is the main stage

01:07.760 --> 01:10.230
muda uchibanashi mo yokayoka

01:07.760 --> 01:10.230
That's where we can chat idly

01:10.230 --> 01:12.590
oato ga mata yoroshikute

01:10.230 --> 01:12.590
Thank you kindly for your attention

01:12.590 --> 01:15.260
osaki mo shiroki gokuraku da

01:12.590 --> 01:15.260
I hope it was a good comedy

01:15.260 --> 01:17.610
gokuraku da gokuraku da

01:15.260 --> 01:17.610
A comedy, a comedy

01:17.610 --> 01:20.760
arayotto gokuraku joudo ringu

01:17.610 --> 01:20.760
A comedy from the comedy heaven

01:20.760 --> 01:23.100
chin-ton chin-ton-shan

01:20.760 --> 01:23.100
Twing-twang twing-twang-twong

01:33.700 --> 01:37.030
"Where did you get this pike from?"

01:37.030 --> 01:40.220
"From the Nihonbashi riverside fish market, my lord."

01:40.220 --> 01:42.110
Then the lord sa--

01:45.310 --> 01:48.280
"Meguro's pike is really the best.

01:48.940 --> 01:51.270
Thank you... kindly... for your attention...

01:57.130 --> 01:59.140
Ruined

02:05.630 --> 02:07.440
What's wrong, Marii?

02:07.770 --> 02:10.650
They started clapping before I even finished!

02:10.650 --> 02:13.040
They clapped before the punchline!

02:13.040 --> 02:15.030
That should come after the punchline!

02:15.350 --> 02:17.760
Doesn't that mean you're so bad they just wanna get rid of you?

02:17.760 --> 02:18.740
What?!

02:19.010 --> 02:24.060
There are all kinds of guests. Some might not know when to clap.

02:24.060 --> 02:25.700
Did something like that ever happen to you?

02:25.700 --> 02:26.580
Just the other day...

02:26.920 --> 02:31.070
"Live long, live long and prosper. May great wealth await for you..."

02:34.000 --> 02:37.170
"...for you wherever you go, even different lands and skies.

02:37.170 --> 02:39.270
May you always have..."

02:41.590 --> 02:45.070
"have your daily bread and always be brimming full of life.

02:45.070 --> 02:50.060
Like the long-lived king Shuringan and his dear wife Gurindai, and their children..."

02:50.060 --> 02:52.240
Clap when I'm done for Christ's sake!

02:52.240 --> 02:54.760
The other guests felt like they had to clap too!

02:54.760 --> 02:57.200
They missed the most important part of the whole story!

02:57.200 --> 02:59.100
It's the perfect way to mess up a joke!

02:59.100 --> 03:00.700
That's almost like some kind of terrorist attack.

03:00.700 --> 03:01.530
How terrible...

03:01.530 --> 03:03.660
People who do that should just drop dead!

03:03.930 --> 03:08.410
But then you'd end up dead too!

03:08.410 --> 03:13.380
Just the other day, I gave Marii my spare ticket to a classical concert.

03:21.370 --> 03:25.090
But the piece wasn't even over yet! It was so embarrassing!

03:25.090 --> 03:29.660
The main theme comes after those few seconds of silence! She ruined it!

03:29.660 --> 03:33.470
It's not like Marii did it intentionally though. I think you can excuse her.

03:33.470 --> 03:36.400
For example, it's not obvious when to clap while listening to Tchaikovsky.

03:36.680 --> 03:40.560
There are people out there who mislead laughter and feelings.

03:40.560 --> 03:42.800
I learned that the hard way too.

03:42.800 --> 03:47.290
Just the other day, I gave Marii my spare ticket to a baseball game.

03:54.420 --> 03:57.840
She tried to start the wave at the wrong time!

03:58.460 --> 04:02.090
That can get everyone fired up if you do it at the right time! She ruined it!

04:02.390 --> 04:05.690
It's not like Marii did it intentionally though.

04:05.690 --> 04:07.600
Not like that makes it any better.

04:07.920 --> 04:10.970
But there aren't many chances when they can't score points.

04:10.970 --> 04:15.650
For example, it's hard to find the right time to do the wave at a Kyunichi Drag-ons match.

04:16.080 --> 04:18.630
Mind if I butt in?

04:18.630 --> 04:19.730
You're the district organizer.

04:20.050 --> 04:24.000
Just the other day, Marii helped out at the festival.

04:24.000 --> 04:25.520
Then, when it was over...

04:25.520 --> 04:27.200
Thanks for your help today!

04:27.670 --> 04:30.430
Let's close it with a clap!

04:30.430 --> 04:31.830
Ready!

04:34.410 --> 04:35.420
You were way too early!

04:35.770 --> 04:38.630
I was still saying "ready"! You ruined it!

04:38.630 --> 04:39.800
Really?

04:40.090 --> 04:42.210
Mind if I butt in?

04:42.210 --> 04:43.470
It's a neighborhood manga artist.

04:43.470 --> 04:44.900
There was this time...

04:48.380 --> 04:51.200
His hakama's... striped!

04:53.630 --> 04:55.840
You laughed at the wrong part!

04:55.840 --> 04:57.270
That part isn't even funny!

04:57.550 --> 04:59.150
And then at the part where you should have laughed...

05:06.180 --> 05:08.590
His hakama's... striped!

05:08.590 --> 05:10.690
Why are you laughing at that?!

05:10.690 --> 05:12.020
What's funny about his pants?!

05:12.020 --> 05:13.750
Don't laugh when it isn't even funny!

05:14.020 --> 05:16.230
In your case, I'd be happy anyone found it funny at all.

05:16.230 --> 05:18.080
Well, I guess that's one way to look at it.

05:19.450 --> 05:21.850
Oh come on, shut up already.

05:21.850 --> 05:24.260
Who cares if my timing's off a bit?

05:24.260 --> 05:27.180
If only it was just a bit. But what you're doing is like...

05:32.540 --> 05:34.310
Heaven and earth are calling me!

05:34.310 --> 05:37.230
I come to defeat evil, for I am--

05:42.030 --> 05:44.690
It's like attacking the hero during his transformation scene!

05:46.140 --> 05:47.990
I-Is it that bad?!

05:47.990 --> 05:50.450
Yes. That's what it means to mess up the timing.

05:50.790 --> 05:54.910
I'll train Marii to know the right timing and mend her rhythm!

05:53.160 --> 05:54.910
Mend
her
rhythm

05:55.260 --> 05:57.120
Pounding time!

05:57.390 --> 05:59.380
It'll hurt a lot if you miss the timing!

06:01.420 --> 06:03.620
I can't even watch this!

06:03.620 --> 06:05.880
Does it have to be so dangerous?

06:05.880 --> 06:08.240
Couldn't you use some cuter method like they do with kids?

06:08.240 --> 06:11.430
We could make her "catch" the rhythm if we were a band or something.

06:11.740 --> 06:16.890
To make Marii mend her rhythm, we must be ready to face even death itself!

06:17.180 --> 06:20.900
Oh how serious and hard the way of the rhythm is!

06:21.110 --> 06:22.400
Here we go!

06:29.610 --> 06:32.240
Don't move your hand when it's safe!

06:32.240 --> 06:33.950
It's not like I'm doing it intentionally...

06:34.220 --> 06:37.780
It's weird that her timing is so off in every way.

06:37.780 --> 06:39.400
There must be a reason for it.

06:39.400 --> 06:40.920
Well, she's also tone deaf.

06:42.400 --> 06:44.880
What if she has no sense of rhythm in the first place?

06:44.880 --> 06:46.920
Metronome!

06:47.290 --> 06:50.180
Improve your sense of rhythm with this!

07:04.940 --> 07:05.580
I see!

07:05.580 --> 07:09.070
She fell into hypnosis before she could improve her rhythm!

07:09.340 --> 07:10.280
Then what if...

07:10.680 --> 07:11.990
Ready!

07:12.940 --> 07:14.590
Perfect timing!

07:14.590 --> 07:16.370
It's not what we were going for, but it worked!

07:16.370 --> 07:18.450
What about manga? Can she read it like a normal person now?

07:24.120 --> 07:25.920
She isn't laughing at random stuff anymore!

07:25.920 --> 07:28.070
Hell, she isn't laughing at all!

07:28.070 --> 07:29.170
That's normal.

07:30.010 --> 07:31.070
Okay, let's pound mochi!

07:31.070 --> 07:32.390
Come on, Marii!

07:40.710 --> 07:43.020
Her timing's perfect!

07:43.270 --> 07:46.380
But what will happen when we wake her up?

07:52.460 --> 07:54.480
Are you okay, Marii?

07:54.480 --> 07:57.950
Thanks to my hospital visit, I know why my timing is always so off!

07:58.950 --> 08:02.230
I noticed that my EKG was totally messed up!

08:02.230 --> 08:04.290
I'm so relieved to know that my timing is messed up because of my heart!

08:04.610 --> 08:06.000
Ah, that's grea--

08:06.000 --> 08:08.210
Wait, Marii, that's arrhythmia!

08:12.150 --> 08:15.790
Luckily, they said it's not that serious and it's stable for now.

08:15.790 --> 08:19.100
We were so worried about you, Marii!

08:20.240 --> 08:23.060
His hakama's... striped!

08:23.060 --> 08:26.480
It's not her arrhythmia, is it?

08:33.690 --> 08:35.390
So this is Jinbocho!

08:35.390 --> 08:37.370
I'm getting vibes of business success!

08:37.370 --> 08:40.330
It's also called the town of students and books.

08:40.450 --> 08:43.290
Grande

08:40.720 --> 08:43.290
There are many publishers, bookstores and universities around here.

08:41.330 --> 08:43.290
Haga Bookstore

08:41.950 --> 08:43.290
Senshu University

08:43.590 --> 08:45.520
I wanna walk around checking out antique bookstores!

08:45.520 --> 08:46.990
That sounds good!

08:47.750 --> 08:48.860
Hold your horses!

08:48.860 --> 08:50.880
One can't fight on an empty stomach!

08:50.880 --> 08:53.630
There are many good restaurants around here.

08:54.050 --> 08:56.510
Tendon, western cuisine, curry...

08:56.510 --> 09:01.600
Also, because publishers work late, the Chinese restaurants stay open late as well.

09:01.600 --> 09:06.390
Having lunch sounds good, but shouldn't we drop in to say hi first?

09:06.390 --> 09:07.720
Say hi to whom?

09:07.720 --> 09:10.240
The publisher that takes care of us.

09:11.530 --> 09:12.740
Got'cha!

09:12.740 --> 09:14.530
That's a showdown.

09:14.530 --> 09:16.530
Three Bookstores

09:16.530 --> 09:19.450
Um, I think it's that way!

09:20.250 --> 09:21.370
Found it!

09:23.870 --> 09:26.330
Hang in there!

09:26.330 --> 09:27.510
Wait, we're wrong here!

09:26.330 --> 09:30.290
Shogakukan Bld.

09:27.510 --> 09:29.270
This's Shogakukan!

09:29.270 --> 09:30.290
Oh, you're right!

09:30.290 --> 09:33.210
Our publisher's Kodansha!

09:33.210 --> 09:34.720
How could you mess that up?

09:34.720 --> 09:39.220
When I looked up that manga artist from the neighborhood, it said his debut was in Sunday!

09:41.220 --> 09:43.300
We should hurry over to Kodansha.

09:43.300 --> 09:44.200
Hold your horses!

09:44.200 --> 09:46.390
Let's not ignore Shogakukan!

09:46.390 --> 09:53.110
Their elementary school textbooks and magazines contribute greatly to the intellectual growth of children!

09:53.110 --> 09:56.450
They teach us everything important in life!

09:56.680 --> 09:58.740
Friendship! Determination! Victory!

09:58.740 --> 10:03.280
Shogakukan teaches and leads children! And that's not all!

10:03.280 --> 10:04.580
You're going overboard with the praise.

10:04.580 --> 10:07.920
Not to mention friendship, determination and victory are Jump.

10:07.920 --> 10:11.970
The Sunday magazine would embody love, youth and Conan, wouldn't it?

10:11.970 --> 10:13.420
Shueisha is that way!

10:14.540 --> 10:15.960
So this is Shueisha!

10:15.960 --> 10:17.970
The building smells of money.

10:17.970 --> 10:21.100
Some people just call it the One Piece building.

10:21.100 --> 10:26.520
Is there a Dragon Ball building and a Seiya building too?

10:26.930 --> 10:28.230
What about the Hunter building?

10:30.470 --> 10:32.170
Is there a Hunter building?

10:34.160 --> 10:38.220
There were holdups, so construction work is probably ongoing.

10:38.220 --> 10:40.400
This business deals in culture! Yeah!

10:40.400 --> 10:42.660
The goal is to publish things that contribute to society!

10:43.020 --> 10:46.670
"Publishing is planting seeds that will bear great fruits in life!"

10:46.670 --> 10:51.610
That's what someone said at Shueisha, which belongs to the Hitotsubashi Group!

10:51.610 --> 10:52.590
Hitotsubashi?

10:52.590 --> 10:58.080
A group of publishing companies led by Shogakukan, including Shueisha, Hakusensha, Shodensha, and so on.

10:58.080 --> 11:01.550
Yeah, that's the Hitotsubashi Group, but weren't we going to Kodansha?

11:00.550 --> 11:01.550
Tokyo, Bunkyo, Otowa 2-12-21
For telephone numbers, please
refer to the table of contents.

11:01.550 --> 11:02.710
That's right.

11:02.710 --> 11:04.010
Let's go!

11:04.680 --> 11:08.650
It's quite unimpressive when compared to Jinbocho.

11:08.650 --> 11:10.590
There aren't any shops, either...

11:10.590 --> 11:12.960
But there's a famous temple!

11:12.960 --> 11:14.900
The Gokoku temple which this station is named after!

11:15.190 --> 11:16.140
And here it is.

11:16.140 --> 11:19.650
They say Tokugawa Tsunayoshi built it because his mother told him so.

11:19.650 --> 11:21.680
Oh, he had an Oedipus complex?

11:21.680 --> 11:23.390
He was a furry too.

11:24.720 --> 11:27.120
He's famous for his Edicts on Compassion for Living Things.

11:27.430 --> 11:32.580
It sure is an impressive, old building, but it's not really one for the 21st century generation.

11:32.580 --> 11:34.210
That's not true!

11:34.210 --> 11:38.940
The funeral of that guy who stole a bike was held here too!

11:39.840 --> 11:42.760
A legendary number of people were attending!

11:43.140 --> 11:47.290
Also this is the final resting place of the number one Karate Maniac, President Oyama Masutatsu,

11:47.290 --> 11:50.140
and of the great Kajiwara Ikki as well!

11:51.000 --> 11:55.400
Mr. Kajiwara basically built a few of the Kodansha buildings!

11:55.400 --> 11:57.360
Let's go to Kodansha!

11:59.580 --> 12:04.290
Kodansha. Formed as the Imperial Japanese Oratorical Society.

12:04.290 --> 12:08.690
They published the Kodan Club entertainment magazine.

12:08.690 --> 12:12.720
Later it was renamed the Imperial Japanese Oratorical Society Kodansha.

12:12.720 --> 12:14.200
Thus is born the name of the company.

12:14.200 --> 12:14.960
That's so long!

12:14.960 --> 12:17.290
So long and so many strokes on the characters!

12:14.960 --> 12:19.050
Great Japan
Oratorical Society
Kodansha

12:17.290 --> 12:18.490
Were they misfits or what?!

12:19.050 --> 12:22.930
Makes sense! So that's why Kodansha's misfit mangas are so successful!

12:22.930 --> 12:24.760
They empathized.

12:26.340 --> 12:30.390
It's really worth checking out the paintings of the former company presidents in the great hall.

12:34.300 --> 12:36.450
They're all called Noma.

12:37.070 --> 12:40.110
I've got this faint sense of deja-vu...

12:40.110 --> 12:41.570
What do you mean?

12:41.570 --> 12:47.490
I may be wrong, but it feels like not very long ago we had some event here.

12:47.780 --> 12:53.620
Something about five voice actresses in a talk-show and signing posters...

12:53.970 --> 12:55.250
I remember!

12:56.580 --> 13:00.300
They were attending the funeral of Rikiishi Toru!

13:00.300 --> 13:02.100
Rikiishi? Who's that?

13:02.100 --> 13:04.590
The greatest rival of Tomorrow's Joe!

13:04.590 --> 13:06.680
The funeral was led by Terayama Shuji!

13:06.680 --> 13:09.680
He's the one who sees a foggy ocean the moment he strikes a match!

13:11.860 --> 13:16.040
In more modern terms, the kind of person who'd mourn Mami or Fire Fist Ace?

13:17.180 --> 13:18.980
By the way, how old were you again, Kigu?

13:19.370 --> 13:22.050
Not old enough to get wrinkles! Tee-hee!

13:22.480 --> 13:27.160
I wonder if Mr. Noma's on the top floor now, sipping wine with a cat on his lap?

13:27.160 --> 13:31.840
I can hear him saying "In the spring rain, the scent of Venus's sigh reaches me."

13:31.840 --> 13:34.460
Mr. Kibayashi would do that, not him.

13:34.460 --> 13:37.210
Surprisingly, the president's office is on a lower level, they say.

13:37.210 --> 13:38.870
Huh? Why?

13:38.870 --> 13:43.440
Supposedly its shorter to the fire escape from there.

13:44.500 --> 13:47.720
There's no escape in the magazine's editorial section, by the way.

13:49.430 --> 13:50.540
Hey!

13:50.540 --> 13:51.820
Good afternoon!

13:52.950 --> 13:53.750
Hello.

13:57.160 --> 14:00.600
What's this? Is this some kind of hotel?

14:01.820 --> 14:03.940
There's a café upstairs.

14:05.000 --> 14:06.410
Are they models?

14:06.410 --> 14:09.950
They publish ViVi, and other fashion magazines as well.

14:10.480 --> 14:12.010
That's so classy.

14:12.010 --> 14:16.310
God damn! The building smells of money and it's full of pretty models!

14:16.310 --> 14:18.870
I'm so damn envious!

14:18.870 --> 14:23.110
I hope our editors at Betsu-Maga have some nice offices too!

14:30.470 --> 14:31.780
What the hell's this place?

14:31.780 --> 14:34.430
It's dirty, dangerous and demeaning! The real 3D!

14:34.430 --> 14:48.400
Anoingu

14:34.710 --> 14:43.160
The light and fun Bessatsu Shonen Magazine is built on the daily sacrifice of the editors!

14:45.810 --> 14:47.920
Thank you kindly.

14:51.170 --> 14:57.040
Kumagorou the bear kept walking and walking, but he just couldn't find the place.

14:57.040 --> 15:01.350
"Did I lose my way? I must still be groggy from my long winter sleep."

15:01.350 --> 15:04.510
Then suddenly it came to him in a flash of realization.

15:04.510 --> 15:09.150
"Oh, my! That wasn't winter sleep, it was cold sleep!"

15:10.080 --> 15:11.880
Thank you kindly for your attention.

15:13.350 --> 15:15.350
Surprise Focus

15:15.670 --> 15:18.740
What? The animator ran away?

15:18.740 --> 15:20.350
He wouldn't open his door when you knocked?

15:20.350 --> 15:21.810
Don't give me that!

15:21.810 --> 15:23.030
He just locked himself in!

15:23.030 --> 15:25.080
Break the door down and get in there!

15:25.080 --> 15:28.370
But people say he has a habit of running away from his stress!

15:28.370 --> 15:29.800
Who gives a damn?!

15:29.800 --> 15:32.320
All that matters is that we meet the deadlines!

15:32.320 --> 15:34.500
What's Kigu doing?

15:34.500 --> 15:36.950
She said she's learning a new story.

15:37.250 --> 15:40.200
You shouldn't focus too hard. It's bad for your body.

15:40.200 --> 15:41.760
Don't strain yourself.

15:41.760 --> 15:44.920
I'm training seriously, unlike the rest of you!

15:44.920 --> 15:46.530
Gotta focus!

15:46.530 --> 15:48.880
You're focusing a bit too much...

15:51.650 --> 15:52.920
She focused too much!

15:52.920 --> 15:55.180
Her facial features got all focused together in the middle!

15:55.480 --> 15:57.490
What? How could this be?!

15:57.490 --> 16:02.810
Whoever heard of someone's face getting focused together?!

16:03.460 --> 16:04.410
I see!

16:04.410 --> 16:08.070
So that's how Acchan ended up like that! She focused too much!

16:08.070 --> 16:10.030
One-two! One-two!

16:10.310 --> 16:13.100
Otherwise, she wouldn't have been able to get the center position!

16:13.100 --> 16:15.820
You need that kind of focus to win the election and graduate!

16:15.820 --> 16:17.990
Otherwise Den-O won't take you home!

16:18.700 --> 16:20.910
If you focus that much, Kigu,

16:20.910 --> 16:24.300
your graduation ceremony might exceed the 916 multiplier!

16:24.300 --> 16:28.360
I don't want to graduate or focus or study in New York!

16:28.360 --> 16:32.930
I drew you a shoebill to help lower your focus!

16:33.240 --> 16:36.250
You can't break my focus with something like that!

16:36.250 --> 16:38.260
But it's the coolest bird ever...

16:38.260 --> 16:40.630
Would you prefer one in profile?

16:40.630 --> 16:45.710
But it's famous for catching fish by surprise, so I'll just end up focusing on when it moves!

16:46.340 --> 16:48.690
Try massaging your face to loosen up.

16:49.180 --> 16:50.150
Okay.

16:50.570 --> 16:52.560
Am I still focused?

16:52.560 --> 16:54.480
Your face is back to normal,

16:54.480 --> 16:57.620
but because of all the focusing you did, now you've got focus lines surrounding you.

16:58.660 --> 17:00.420
They won't disappear!

17:00.420 --> 17:04.000
I don't wanna be focused on, but because of the focus lines, everyone focuses on me!

17:04.000 --> 17:07.200
Kigu, let's have a coffee break and relax.

17:07.200 --> 17:08.750
I got some chocolate as a present the other day.

17:11.360 --> 17:12.760
It's so sweet!

17:14.670 --> 17:15.720
This is so calming!

17:16.140 --> 17:17.670
It's not getting any better.

17:17.670 --> 17:19.570
I'm totally relaxed!

17:19.570 --> 17:22.060
It doesn't look like that at all.

17:22.350 --> 17:24.680
The focus lines just won't disappear.

17:24.680 --> 17:27.300
Now it's like a manga by Mr. Shimamoto.

17:27.300 --> 17:31.440
Ah, that style that makes even the most insignificant lines dramatic.

17:31.900 --> 17:35.680
Should we just call ourselves the Rakugo Performers of Fire?

17:35.680 --> 17:37.680
We could be members of a high school or university rakugo club,

17:37.680 --> 17:39.950
working as hard as we can to fulfill our dreams.

17:40.530 --> 17:43.550
Let's not. We're not fiery enough for that.

17:43.550 --> 17:48.970
But this way we'll have to put up with the focus lines no matter what we say!

17:48.970 --> 17:49.710
Even in love...

17:52.860 --> 17:54.380
You know, I think...

17:55.390 --> 17:56.320
I love you!

18:02.260 --> 18:04.570
I don't want to be in a suffocating love story like that!

18:04.570 --> 18:08.020
That was the first time the focus lines really matched the tension!

18:08.020 --> 18:10.160
I'm not happy about that at all!

18:10.160 --> 18:11.810
There's no need to be angry...

18:11.810 --> 18:15.150
I'm not angry! It just looks that way!

18:15.520 --> 18:17.740
And it wouldn't just affect your love.

18:18.220 --> 18:19.490
It'd happen when you read poems,

18:19.820 --> 18:21.240
or cleaned your ears,

18:21.590 --> 18:22.990
or took a bath,

18:23.420 --> 18:24.620
or died...

18:24.620 --> 18:26.830
I don't want such a suffocating life!

18:26.830 --> 18:29.580
It reminds me of Dezaki's work, so I quite like it.

18:29.580 --> 18:32.500
Do you mean stuff like this?!

18:32.920 --> 18:34.000
And this?!

18:34.380 --> 18:36.670
And even this?!

18:36.990 --> 18:38.210
Just give up.

18:38.210 --> 18:41.640
Kigu, you'll never have a background like the one I'm about to show you.

18:46.110 --> 18:47.000
I love you!

18:48.480 --> 18:49.730
That's so unfair!

18:49.730 --> 18:51.760
I want a background like that too!

18:51.760 --> 18:53.090
Is that envy I hear?

18:53.090 --> 18:56.690
That pink, fluffy style doesn't suit you at all, though.

18:56.940 --> 18:58.200
The hell'd you just say?!

18:58.440 --> 19:00.320
I said it doesn't suit you.

19:00.570 --> 19:01.320
I'll kick your ass!

19:01.320 --> 19:04.360
Could it be that Marii can't get rid of hers either?

19:04.360 --> 19:06.200
That's not funny!

19:06.460 --> 19:08.000
Yep, it's still there.

19:08.000 --> 19:12.630
Marii, you might have to live your whole life in that pink, fluffy atmosphere!

19:12.970 --> 19:14.060
What?!

19:14.600 --> 19:15.840
Even if you get beaten up,

19:16.990 --> 19:18.470
or run over by a car,

19:19.320 --> 19:21.760
or something falls and hits you in the head,

19:22.200 --> 19:23.390
or when you die.

19:23.390 --> 19:25.310
That's beyond a joke!

19:25.310 --> 19:27.970
Why would anything fall on my head in the first place?!

19:28.240 --> 19:32.250
Well, I don't think you'd have too much trouble living a pink, fluffy life like that.

19:32.250 --> 19:33.860
The real problem here is Kigu.

19:33.860 --> 19:34.650
Yeah!

19:35.040 --> 19:36.890
Hey! I've got problems too!

19:36.890 --> 19:38.780
You look perfectly at peace to me.

19:39.010 --> 19:42.360
Anyway, the moral of the story is that too much focus is never good.

19:43.080 --> 19:46.480
It's very risky how industries focus themselves in Tokyo or how companies focus on trading

19:46.120 --> 19:52.670
Bid
results

19:46.120 --> 19:52.670
Construction company

19:46.120 --> 19:52.670
Bid

19:46.120 --> 19:52.670
Ishida Constr.
Tanaka Constr.
Hirata Co. Ltd.
Haneishi Assoc.

19:46.480 --> 19:48.480
with only a limited set of partners.

19:48.480 --> 19:52.670
Manga artists shouldn't enter into exclusive contracts either.

19:52.940 --> 19:56.630
So many artists have been ruined by those unreasonable conditions!

19:56.890 --> 20:01.380
When blame is focused on one person, he becomes a scapegoat.

20:01.380 --> 20:04.610
When power is focused in the hands of one person, he becomes a dictator.

20:05.140 --> 20:05.180
Love Love Love Love Love Love

20:05.140 --> 20:09.730
When unrequited love is focused too much on one person, that's the birth of a stalker.

20:05.180 --> 20:05.220
Love Love Love Love Love Love

20:10.160 --> 20:13.350
When sales focus too much on one show, it leads to the decline of the industry.

20:13.820 --> 20:17.330
So, Marii, do you understand now how focus can be a problem?

20:17.330 --> 20:18.360
Y-Yeah.

20:18.910 --> 20:22.340
For instance, in prefab bathrooms where the tub and the toilet are focused in one room,

20:22.340 --> 20:25.620
you can't take a leak while someone's using the bath.

20:25.900 --> 20:30.620
And you can't wash yourself off before getting in the tub because the toilet will get wet too.

20:30.620 --> 20:32.120
Yeah, I guess,

20:32.120 --> 20:34.460
though that's a pretty boring, everyday example.

20:34.740 --> 20:36.490
Isn't that great, Marii?

20:37.380 --> 20:41.840
Anyway, the point is that instead of focusing, we need to scatter!

20:42.200 --> 20:45.830
We need you, Marii, since you're so scatterbrained anyway!

20:45.830 --> 20:47.640
Flattery will get you nowhere, you know!

20:47.640 --> 20:48.810
I don't think that was flattery.

20:48.810 --> 20:52.880
Oh, right! We should have separate dressing rooms too!

20:52.880 --> 20:56.350
If we're all in the same room and some rioter breaks in, we're done for!

20:56.650 --> 21:00.240
I'll ask the manager to give us separate rooms!

21:06.140 --> 21:09.580
He said, "Who'd'ya think you are? Shinsuke?!"

21:09.580 --> 21:10.640
Figures.

21:10.640 --> 21:12.660
We've got no choice but to split up this room, then.

21:14.930 --> 21:16.980
This is so boring! I can't take it anymore!

21:16.980 --> 21:19.590
Shut up. This is all for Kigu's sake.

21:19.910 --> 21:21.440
Kigu, are you okay?

21:21.440 --> 21:22.910
It must be rough being in such a cramped space, right?

21:22.910 --> 21:24.300
It's okay!

21:24.300 --> 21:27.010
This cramped space lets me focus like never before!

21:28.220 --> 21:30.110
You mustn't focus!

21:30.110 --> 21:31.930
You have to scatter your thoughts! Unwind!

21:31.930 --> 21:35.640
Yeah! I'm focusing on unwinding!

21:35.640 --> 21:39.120
You mustn't focus on it so intensely!

21:39.120 --> 21:42.110
This has gone beyond the point where we can help her.

21:45.450 --> 21:46.740
Focused Treatment

21:47.740 --> 21:49.200
It all worked out, Kigu.

21:49.200 --> 21:51.310
You're lucky they had focused treatment!

21:51.940 --> 21:54.360
You're much less focused now.

21:54.360 --> 21:57.380
So, can you cure me too?

21:57.380 --> 22:00.460
Sadly, that's beyond the reach of today's medical technology...

22:00.760 --> 22:03.000
Oh, come on! Just cure me!

22:03.000 --> 22:06.410
Marii and the doctor sure do get along well...

22:03.500 --> 22:06.410
I'm terribly sorry, but I can't.

22:06.410 --> 22:07.440
Don't give me that shit!

22:06.890 --> 22:07.440
Yup.

22:07.440 --> 22:09.970
Cure me, you goddamn quack!

22:17.270 --> 22:18.810
jugemu jugemu gokou no surikire

22:17.270 --> 22:18.810
Live long, live long and prosper

22:18.810 --> 22:20.480
kaijari suigyo no suigyou matsu

22:18.810 --> 22:20.480
May great wealth await you wherever you go

22:20.480 --> 22:21.980
unrai matsu fuurai matsu

22:20.480 --> 22:21.980
Even in different lands and under different skies

22:21.980 --> 22:23.440
kuuneru tokoro ni sumu tokoro

22:21.980 --> 22:23.440
May you always have your daily bread

22:23.440 --> 22:24.900
yaburakouji no burakouji

22:23.440 --> 22:24.900
And always be brimming full of life

22:24.900 --> 22:28.200
paipo paipo paipo no shuuringan

22:24.900 --> 22:28.200
Like the long-lived king Shuringan

22:29.200 --> 22:30.950
shuuringan no guurindai

22:29.200 --> 22:30.950
And his dear wife Gurindai

22:30.950 --> 22:33.240
guurindai no ponpokopi no ponpokona no

22:30.950 --> 22:33.240
And their children Ponpokopi and Ponpokona

22:33.240 --> 22:35.450
choukyuumei chousuke

22:33.240 --> 22:35.450
Live a long and blessed life

22:38.330 --> 22:41.420
choi to jikan itadakimasu

22:38.330 --> 22:41.420
Let me have a bit of your time

22:44.170 --> 22:45.840
goseichou kudasai

22:44.170 --> 22:45.840
Please listen closely

22:45.840 --> 22:47.550
A

22:45.840 --> 22:47.550
totonoimashita

22:45.840 --> 22:47.550
We're ready

22:47.550 --> 22:50.260
A

22:47.550 --> 22:50.260
warau koto to kakemashite

22:47.550 --> 22:50.260
You write it "laughing"

22:50.260 --> 22:53.260
A

22:50.260 --> 22:53.260
omatsuri yarou zo tokemasu

22:50.260 --> 22:53.260
You read it "let's party"

22:53.260 --> 22:56.350
A

22:53.260 --> 22:56.350
sono kokoro wa sono kokoro wa

22:53.260 --> 22:56.350
And the point of it is, the point of it is...

22:56.350 --> 22:59.440
A

22:56.350 --> 22:59.440
dochira mo happi ni naru deshou

22:56.350 --> 22:59.440
That everyone will be happy!

22:59.440 --> 23:00.600
A

22:59.440 --> 23:00.600
oato ga yoroshii you de

22:59.440 --> 23:00.600
Thank you kindly for your attention

23:00.600 --> 23:03.520
waraou waraou sa waraimashou

23:00.600 --> 23:03.520
Laugh, laugh, hey, let's laugh

23:03.520 --> 23:06.480
konna jidai koso waraimashou

23:03.520 --> 23:06.480
Life may be hard, but let's laugh

23:06.480 --> 23:07.990
waraou (soiya soiya)

23:06.480 --> 23:07.990
Laugh (yeah yeah)

23:07.990 --> 23:09.530
naitara make da

23:07.990 --> 23:09.530
If you cry, you lose

23:09.530 --> 23:12.700
yakekuso waraimashou

23:09.530 --> 23:12.700
So just laugh until your sides ache

23:12.700 --> 23:15.740
haranbanjou sui mo amai mo

23:12.700 --> 23:15.740
Life may have its ups and downs,

23:15.740 --> 23:18.370
norikoeta appare nipponjin

23:15.740 --> 23:18.370
But great Japanese can get over it

23:18.370 --> 23:21.750
waraou donna toki de mo

23:18.370 --> 23:21.750
Laugh, whatever time may bring

23:21.750 --> 23:24.790
nanikuso waraimashou

23:21.750 --> 23:24.790
Laugh until you run out of breath

23:27.760 --> 23:30.760
kuuki nante yomazu ni warattoke

23:27.760 --> 23:30.760
Who cares where you are? Just laugh

23:30.760 --> 23:33.800
egao (egao) egao (egao)

23:30.760 --> 23:33.800
Smile (smile), smile (smile)

23:33.800 --> 23:36.560
warau kado ni wa fuku kitaru

23:33.800 --> 23:36.560
Smile and the world will smile back at you
